title: EMR Connect › Sites › What each site sees
route: /emr
intro: Record systems belong to a site. 'Clinical record · Site A' and 'Clinical record · Site B' each hold all the programs at their site, and the Billing system serves both. The page lists only the systems at the sites in view, and a viewer limited to one site cannot sync, fix, reconnect, edit or disconnect the other site's system, because it is not there.
dir: TD
also: Demo data. The site view comes from the top bar (a switch for Jordan Perez and Alex Morgan, a locked label for Dr. Rivera and Sam Okafor). Every flow that works on a system (connect, fix, reconnect, sync, disconnect, mappings, write-back) works the same on the systems that are listed.
---
start s1 "Open EMR Connect\nWith Both sites, Site A, Site B, or as Dr. Rivera or Sam Okafor"
decision d1 "Which sites are in view?"

group gBoth "Both sites"
  screen b1 "Jordan Perez or Alex Morgan on 'Both sites'\nThree rows: 'Clinical record · Site A', 'Clinical record · Site B', 'Billing system'\n6 min, 23 charts, 142 files, 2 failures\n'Action required: Billing system needs attention. Also: 2 fields need a mapping...'\nAdvanced: 10 mappings, 2 waiting, 8 log lines"
endgroup

group gA "Site A"
  screen a1 "Dr. Rivera, or Jordan or Alex on 'Site A'\nTwo rows: 'Clinical record · Site A' and 'Billing system'\n6 min, 13 charts, 80 files, 2 failures\n'Action required: Billing system needs attention.'\nAdvanced: 7 mappings, none waiting, 5 log lines"
  process a2 "Site B's record system, its two unmapped fields and its log lines are not listed or counted"
endgroup

group gB "Site B"
  screen c1 "Sam Okafor, or Jordan or Alex on 'Site B'\nTwo rows: 'Clinical record · Site B' and 'Billing system'\n11 min, 10 charts, 62 files, 2 failures\n'Action required: Billing system needs attention. Also: 2 fields need a mapping...'\nAdvanced: 5 mappings, 2 waiting, 3 log lines"
  process c2 "Site A's record system and its log lines are not listed or counted"
endgroup

process tag "For a viewer with both sites on one site, the title carries a small 'Site A' or 'Site B' tag\nThe Connection health line says which site: 'Site A. 1 of 2 systems connected...'"
process note "For a one-site viewer the line has an info icon\n'A record system belongs to a site. You see Site A's record system and the billing system both sites share. The other site's record system is not shown, and you cannot change it.'"
process sum "Charts and files: Site A plus Site B always equals Both sites\nSync failures count each system once: the shared Billing system shows its 2 in every view"

click cSync "Click 'Sync now' in the header (one site in view)"
store sy "Only the systems in view sync\nOnly that site's charts and files go up; the other site's stay as they were\nThe log line is about that site"

click cConn "Click 'Connect a system'"
input pick "Choose the site it serves\nA viewer with both sites: 'Site A', 'Site B' or 'Both sites'\nA one-site viewer: only their own site, as text"
store ns "The new system is listed for that site only\nA system connected as Sam Okafor for Site B never shows for Dr. Rivera"

click cSw "Switch the viewer or the site while a pop-up or the Manage drawer is open for a system that leaves the view"
process gone "The drawer or pop-up closes: it is only drawn for a system in view\nThe store also refuses a change to a system at a site the viewer cannot see"

goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Choose the system and contact"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › What other screens use from EMR Connect"
goto g3 "Continues in: Who can see what › Roles, sites and a record at the other site"
end e1 "Each viewer sees and changes only the systems at their sites"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|Both sites| b1
d1 -->|Site A| a1 --> a2
d1 -->|Site B| c1 --> c2
b1 & a2 & c2 --> tag --> note --> sum
sum --> cSync --> sy
sum --> cConn --> pick --> ns
sy & ns --> e1
cSw --> gone --> e1
pick -.-> g1
sy -.-> g2
e1 --> g3
